1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:01,695
Just five villages…

2
00:00:01,695 --> 00:00:05,446
five villages could have stopped
the Mahabharata war.

3
00:00:05,446 --> 00:00:07,524
And Duryodhana knew it.

4
00:00:07,734 --> 00:00:09,594
This story of Duryodhana…

5
00:00:09,594 --> 00:00:14,621
is our story too. We know what's
right… and still.

6
00:00:14,631 --> 00:00:17,271
In the full court, his mother
Gandhari pleaded—

7
00:00:17,271 --> 00:00:20,326
share the kingdom, rule in peace.

8
00:00:20,326 --> 00:00:24,696
Duryodhana said— not even land the
size of a needle's tip…

9
00:00:24,696 --> 00:00:26,061
will I give.

10
00:00:26,171 --> 00:00:28,611
Tradition remembers his words—

11
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:31,837
I know what is right…
but I can't follow it.

12
00:00:32,037 --> 00:00:35,417
Then at Kurukshetra… Arjuna asked
Krishna the same thing—

13
00:00:35,417 --> 00:00:38,475
why do we do wrong, even
when we don't want to?

14
00:00:38,775 --> 00:00:41,005
It is desire, it is anger…

15
00:00:41,005 --> 00:00:47,410
born of restless passion.
All-devouring… know it as the
enemy here.

16
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:49,720
Krishna says—

17
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:52,380
this is desire, this is anger…

18
00:00:52,380 --> 00:00:54,119
know it as your enemy.

19
00:00:54,119 --> 00:00:55,639
Kama means desire…

20
00:00:55,639 --> 00:00:59,159
krodha means anger.
And the Gita says—

21
00:00:59,159 --> 00:01:01,275
anger is born from desire.

22
00:01:01,375 --> 00:01:03,545
So today, when that pull comes…

23
00:01:03,545 --> 00:01:06,185
pause, and name it—

24
00:01:06,185 --> 00:01:10,848
is this desire, or anger? Name it…
and the choice is yours.

25
00:01:11,668 --> 00:01:13,618
Duryodhana knew…

26
00:01:13,618 --> 00:01:16,588
but didn't stop.
Which is your enemy—

27
00:01:16,588 --> 00:01:18,396
desire, or anger?
